# PostPylot — UI & Design

Design direction: **"Utility meets luxury."** Pro-tool density and precision on the
dashboard; cinematic drama on the landing. OLED black canvas, high-voltage neon lime
accent, generous rounded cards.

Premium references for feel and interaction quality: Linear, Vercel, Raycast, Notion,
Framer, Stripe. Borrow their polish and restraint — do NOT replace PostPylot's established
brand system (OLED black + lime, Syne/Jakarta) with theirs.

## Color Palette

Neon lime on OLED black. **Never reintroduce blue, cyan, or purple as brand colors.**
All colors are CSS variables in `apps/web/src/app/globals.css` — use tokens, not raw hex.

| Role | Token | Dark (default) | Light |
|------|-------|----------------|-------|
| Canvas | `--background` | `#0A0A0A` | `#F5F5F5` |
| Surface / card / sidebar | `--card` `--sidebar` | `#141414` | `#FFFFFF` |
| Raised / muted | `--muted` | `#1A1A1A` | `#EEEEEE` |
| Border / input | `--border` `--input` | `#2A2A2A` | `#E5E5E5` |
| Primary (brand accent) | `--primary` | `#C8FF00` | `#C8FF00` |
| On-primary | `--primary-foreground` | `#0A0A0A` | `#0A0A0A` |
| Text | `--foreground` | `#FFFFFF` | `#0A0A0A` |
| Secondary text | `--muted-foreground` | `#8A8A8A` | `#5C5C5C` |
| Success | `--success` | `#22C55E` | `#16A34A` |
| Warning | `--warning` | `#F59E0B` | `#D97706` |
| Error | `--destructive` | `#EF4444` | `#DC2626` |

- Brand accent (`#C8FF00`) is the single hero color. Use sparingly for emphasis: CTAs,
  active states, key metrics, focus rings, glow.
- **Primary CTAs = solid lime pill with black text** (`bg-primary text-primary-foreground`).
- Brand gradient (`.bg-postpylot-gradient` / `.text-postpylot-gradient`) is lime →
  `#E8FF66`. Use only for the logo mark and rare accents, not as a general background.
- Platform brand colors (YouTube red, LinkedIn/Facebook blue) are allowed only on their
  own platform icons.

## Theming (light + dark)

- Both themes are required. `next-themes` drives the `.dark` class (`attribute="class"`,
  `defaultTheme="dark"`, `enableSystem`).
- Provider: `apps/web/src/components/theme-provider.tsx`; toggle:
  `apps/web/src/components/theme-toggle.tsx` (in the dashboard topbar).
- Never hardcode `dark`-only colors in components. Use tokens so both themes work.
- PWA `theme_color` / `background_color` = `#0A0A0A`; `viewport.themeColor` is
  per-scheme (light `#F5F5F5`, dark `#0A0A0A`).

## Typography

Fonts load in `apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx` via `next/font/google`.

- Display / headings: **Syne** (`--font-syne`, `font-heading`, applied to `h1–h6`)
- Body / UI: **Plus Jakarta Sans** (`--font-jakarta`, `--font-sans`)
- Technical / AI accent: **JetBrains Mono** (`--font-jetbrains-mono`, `font-mono`)
- Headings use tight tracking (`-0.02em`). Do not fall back to Inter / system defaults.

## Radius

Base `--radius` is `1.25rem` — cards and controls are noticeably rounded (bento-box feel).
Prefer `rounded-xl` / `rounded-2xl` on cards; pill (`rounded-full`) only for lime CTAs and chips.

## Landing Page (`/`) — 12 Sections

Navbar → Hero → Problem → Solution Pipeline → Platforms → AI Video → TikTok →
Dashboard Preview → Automation Rules → Pricing/Beta → Final CTA → Footer

**Hero copy:** "Your AI content engine on autopilot."
**Subcopy:** Generate, schedule, publish, and track across YouTube, TikTok, LinkedIn, and Facebook.
**CTAs:** "Launch PostPylot" (→ `/login`), "Watch Demo"

- Hero is brand-first: PostPylot must read as a hero-level signal, one headline, one
  supporting line, one CTA group, one dominant visual. No stat strips or floating badges
  over hero media.

**Pipeline animation (scroll-triggered):** Topic → Research → Writer → Image/Thumbnail →
Video → Scheduler → Publisher → Analytics

Show X/Twitter as "Coming later".

## Landing Animation Rules

- Motion (Framer Motion) for entrances; GSAP for complex scroll triggers; Lenis for smooth scroll.
- Lazy-load heavy animation; no layout shift; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Phase-gated (not MVP): Lottie for small looping/empty-state animations, Rive for
  interactive onboarding illustrations/mascots, Konva for the thumbnail/graphic editor, and
  a command palette. Do not add these until their phase.
- Cinematic black + lime bloom: glassmorphism cards, lime glow orbs, floating dashboard
  preview. Glow uses lime (`rgba(200,255,0,...)`), never blue/cyan/violet.

## Dashboard UI Rules

- Pro-tool aesthetic modeled on high-end fintech/automotive dashboards: OLED/charcoal
  surfaces, large rounded solid cards (not glassmorphism), slim icon sidebar.
- Active nav item = **lime icon**; big bold metrics; lime CTAs with black text.
- Sidebar + topbar + mobile nav; theme toggle in topbar.
- Subtle card entrance, hover lift, skeleton loaders, progress bars, confetti on success.
- No heavy 3D in dashboard. Mobile-first PWA layouts.

## PWA Manifest

```ts
{ name: "PostPylot", short_name: "PostPylot", start_url: "/dashboard",
  display: "standalone", theme_color: "#0A0A0A", background_color: "#0A0A0A",
  orientation: "portrait" }
```

Icons: `public/icons/icon-{72,96,128,144,152,192,384,512}x512.png`, generated from
`public/icon.svg` + `public/icon-maskable.svg` via `scripts/generate-icons.mjs` (lime
mark on `#0A0A0A`). Regenerate PNGs after changing the SVGs.

## Accessibility

Semantic HTML, keyboard nav, visible focus, sufficient contrast, alt text, ARIA only when
needed. Lime `#C8FF00` on black passes contrast; on light surfaces use black text on lime,
never lime text on white.
